  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 VDocs – Release Notes\n\t\t🚀 Version: 2026.10.2\n         This release brings full Open XML theme mapping, a refreshed XML documentation surface across the DOM, and a substantial unit‑test addition covering the new theme pipeline.\n\t\t \n         ✨ Added\n\t\t \n          - Theme mapping (OOXML ⇄ DOM)\n           \n          - New XML.DOMExtensions.ThemeEx extension class with MapToModel / MapToXml methods.\n           \n          - Full support for the three OOXML theme schemes\n          \n          - Round‑trip support: themes can be read from OOXML and serialised back with the same shape and attribute values.\n          \n          - Angle conversion (1/60000 of a degree) and EMU widths/distances handled transparently\n          \n         - Documentation\n           \n          - Comprehensive XML doc comments added across the DOM:\n          \n          - Base and infrastructure: BaseElement, BaseFill, BaseGraphicElement, BaseStyle, BaseTextStyle, BaseTableElement, Element, ParentElement, FontPart, DocumentHeaderFooterPart.\n           \n          - Measurement units: DocumentUnit, FontSize, Percentage, Rotation.\n           \n          - Styles: BorderStyle, BaseDocumentStyle, BuiltInStyle, ConditionalFormatStyle, DocumentDefualtStyles, DocumentStyles, EffectExtent, EffectStyle, FillStyleList, Font, FontScheme, FormatScheme, Languages, Margin, PageBorders, ParagraphBorders, ParagraphIndentation, ParagraphStyle, RectBorder, ScriptFont, Spacing, Tab, TableBaseStyle, TableBorder, TableCellStyle, TableLook, TableRowStyle, TableStyle, TextStyle, Theme, Tile, Underline.\n           \n          - Color classes: BaseColorField, Color, ColorField, ColorScheme, Fill, FillTile, FillToRectangle, Gradient, GradientStop, Hue, IPathShade, LinearShade, Luminance, PathShade, PatternFill, PictureOrTextureFill, Saturation, ZebraColor.\n           \n          - Effect classes: Bevel, Effect3D, Glow, OuterShadow, Reflection, Shading, Shadow, TextEffect, TextOutlineEffect.\n           \n          - Enums: the entire DOM.Enums namespace now has rich summaries, remarks, and at least four usage examples per enum.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
